{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/383876-questions-about-ctd","id":383876,"title":"Questions about CtD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-27T19:02:46-08:00","id":383876,"title":"Questions about CtD","content":"im curious about some things about Changeling, mainly on the relationships between the Changelings and some magical traditions (the hermetic mainly), also<br /> if the changeling dies, the human host forgets Everything about the dreaming. but what happends if the human host dies? what can the changeling Do?.<br /> can a changeling in his real form actually have a child with a human? or it needs to be with the human host?<br /> does the Age of a Changeling shows on its human host or the human host can be very young while the actual changeling be ancient?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":1754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","user":"Crowley","date":". 01-27-2015, 11:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T21:48:20-08:00","id":383991,"title":"","content":"I think... you're interpreting the dual nature of the changeling-human bond a bit too... disparate. While a changeling is technically a fae entity that joins with a human host, they exist as one being; even if what &quot;world&quot; they're interacting with can cause them to bend farther towards one of the two components more strongly.<br /> <br /> The changelings as a whole don't have much dealings with the Traditions. One of the founding Houses of the Order of Hermes was known for interacting with the fae of old, but they have long since fallen into obscurity. The Hollow Ones are probably the group with the most regular dealings with changelings, simply because the Hollow Ones have a thing for getting involved with other supernaturals.<br /> <br /> If the human host dies, commoner kiths reincarnate into a new host. Sidhe die; they don't like this.<br /> <br /> There's nothing stopping a changeling from enchanting a human, and then conceiving a child with them while they're interacting with the changeling side of things.<br /> <br /> The last question... who knows sometimes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T22:29:21-08:00","id":384001,"title":"","content":"what happends when a mage goes to the Dreaming and has sex with a fae on its real form? would a kithain be born or something ...New?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T22:42:56-08:00","id":384003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> if the changeling dies, the human host forgets Everything about the dreaming </div> </div> </div>First of all this would imply either a Chimerical death which is more akin to a coma, for the Fae part of the changeling that is, which is temporary only meaning that after a set time depending on the Changelings Banality the Fae soul once again awakens with all the memories it previously had or you mean the Fae half has been undone by Banality which is more permanent, though arguably depending on the exact nature of this may not be that permanent meaning that a mortal death may release the Fae soul free to reincarnate, but in both of these cases yes the mortal half will not remember anything about the Dreaming thanks to the Mists.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> what happends if the human host dies? </div> </div> </div>Well first of all host is a bad wording on the matter. Changelings, other than the Sidhe who for the most part aren't &quot;proper&quot; Changelings, have become what they are through a Changeling Way ritual that has entwined their Fae soul with that of a mortal meaning that it is not as much a possession as it is one fused soul that has been born the way it is, making the Changeling a half-mortal half-Fea being instead of fully either. So taking this into account if the human part dies, as in the Changeling faces non-Chimerical death, the Fae part dies with it and moves on to reincarnate with the next suitable human soul.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> can a changeling in his real form actually have a child with a human? </div> </div> </div>Yes he can and the child is called Kinain, though thanks to the Mists the human partner won't really remember much of the Changeling unless Enchanted, but the result is the same if the Changeling has a child with a human without showing her/him it's Fae side, which also leaves the mortal with normal recollection of event's.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> it needs to be with the human host? </div> </div> </div>Like mentioned earlier there is no separation between a Changeling and it's human side so even when in their Fae likeness, that is the Changeling has either called upon the Wyrd or Enchanted the human, they are still also their human half thus like said above the results are the same no matter whether the mortal knows s/he is sleeping with a Changeling or not.<br /> <br /> There are only two Fae beings that are fully Fae beings without being tied to a human, and without going into the classification of True Fae for which we have no actual stats unless using DA:F Fae as the True Fae, and for the most part only the other one of them is capable of Possession. These two are the Chimera and the Adhene, the latter of which are very much like Changelings except they have never gone through the Changeling Way ritual and they do have the ability to possess a mortal to shield themselves from Banality but it isn't easy and the mortal must usually be asleep and should it awaken the possessor is generally driven out. You can find more information about the Adhene from <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/111/Denizens-of-the-Dreaming?term=deni&amp;it=1\" target=\"_blank\">Denizens of the Dreaming</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> does the Age of a Changeling shows on its human host or the human host can be very young while the actual changeling be ancient? </div> </div> </div>Usually they are one and the same, like said it's not possession it's fusion of the two souls and beings that has been as it is since birth. But there are arguably exceptions especially depending on ST's take on the matter. For example there are certain Sidhe who age considerably faster unless they regularly practice certain abhorrent ways of attaining Glamour, which again depending on ST can either or even both prevent their fast aging or reverse it altogether, and some might rule this aging to affect both their human sides and their Fae sides equally some might not. I'd err for the side of caution and say that unlike me most ST's probably keep the aging in such cases purely Chimerical though the source material might not be quite so clear cut.<br /> <br /> Then again if you are trying to avoid the ageism trap of CtD then you can unlink the Childing/Wilder/Grump states from Changelings physical Age which could mean that the Fae half can be of seemingly different age than the human side. But this latter part is not in any form canon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> mainly on the relationships between the Changelings and some magical traditions (the hermetic mainly) </div> </div> </div>I'll start this by saying that the Changeling relations with other supernaturals are complicated considerably by the fact that the Mists affect the other supernaturals as easily as they affect mortals that is unless Enchanted the other Supernaturals cannot usually remember the Changelings except as fleeting dreams depending upon their Banality ratings of course. That being said the Hermetics do acknowledge the existence of the Fae and one of their minor Houses that has been absorbed into Ex Miscellania in the modern day, though they are likely to hold on to their own House moniker even within Ex Miscellania as they are separated from the rest by blood, and that is House Merinita which had strong ties to the Fae and their magic many if not most members having been Kinain themselves. I do think that either <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/3046/Guide-to-the-Traditions?term=Guide+to+the+tra&amp;it=1\" target=\"_blank\">Guide to the Traditions</a> or <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/198/Mage-Storytellers-Handbook?cPath=1_6531&amp;it=1\" target=\"_blank\">Mage Storytellers Handbook</a>, revised, mentions them and has some suggestions on how to use them in a Mage game. But in any case House Merinita has traditionally had strong ties with the Fae, and I would think the modern remnants of the House keep up those relations as best they can. As for hte Hermetics at large the Code of Hermes still holds a commandment about not angering the Fae but for most of the Order the time of the Fae has passed and while they once did wield powers to make even the Masters quake in their boots they are mostly believed to be lost now, again see the Mists.<br /> <br /> Some Verbena, again like those with some Fae blood in them, might hold relations similar to the Merinita with the Changelings and the same is true of a some Dreamspeakers perhaps but like said thanks to the Mists even the Mages tend to not know much of the fate of the Fae or even of hte existence of Changelings.<br /> <br /> As a final thing, and this is mentioned both in the TB: OoH and in either the GttT or MSTH regarding House Merinita and that is that their decline in the Order is the result of majority of them retreating into the otherworlds, ie the Dreaming, sometime in the 1300's and that they might still be present there gathering their strength. Similar rumors claim that the Dreaming might act as a refuge for the last surviving members of House Diedne as well which may not bode well for the Order at large.<br /> <br /> So there ya go hope these answers/ramblings are of some use to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T23:07:29-08:00","id":384008,"title":"","content":"One last question.<br /> <br /> a friend told me that Nightmares are quite brutal when it comes to Changeling. that they are particularly nasty when it comes to beings that use Glamour but they are not much of a threat against anything else..how can make a Nightmare that can actually be a threat against mages/werewolves and other supernaturals as well humans?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T03:38:44-08:00","id":384074,"title":"","content":"A Nightmare is just a term for a type of Chimerical Creature that is particularly nasty and born of, you guessed it, nightmares. There are several ways they can REALLY be a threat if the Nightmare is potent enough to create a powerful Chimera since they are capable of existing in the Chimerical reflection of the World and withstanding banality for a length of time actually feeding of the Dark Glamour of Despair and Tragic Misery. They can also, with the right Redes, see everything a Changeling can of the mortal world but the mortal world cannot see them, they can also effect it with Chimerical Redes or Arts and even expend Glamour just like a changeling to use Wyrd Redes and Arts or even make themselves visible and 'real' for a time. But what's more dangerous the Monster you can see or the one you can't? The one you remember or the one that is fleeting to recall as a dream?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T13:03:55-08:00","id":387582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/383876-questions-about-ctd#post383876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">im curious about some things about Changeling, mainly on the relationships between the Changelings and some magical traditions (the hermetic mainly),</div> </div> </div> </div>Certain Mages are more banal than others. Technocracy is prolley the worst as far as banality ratings.<br /> There is some dispute about the SoE. But mostly the traditions will be better. But the Euthantos and yes the hidebound hermetics will be a bit hard on a changeling.<br /> I can't think of where I saw Banality ratings for mages at.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T14:48:18-08:00","id":387634,"title":"","content":"There's a chart of banality ratings for other supernaturals in the back of the 2e core book. I would take it as very loose guidelines/advice though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T03:02:03-08:00","id":391188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/383876-questions-about-ctd#post383876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. . . if the changeling dies, the human host forgets Everything about the dreaming. but what happends if the human host dies? what can the changeling Do?.</div> </div> </div> </div>Commoner (i.e. non-sidhe) changelings and the sidhe of House Scathach went through a ritual around the time of the Shattering (ca. the early Renaissance), making them more like mummies or Celestial Exalted. If the human body dies, the faerie &quot;soul&quot; reincarnates (at some point), bonding with the soul of a newborn human child (often one related to its last incarnation) to create a new changeling. Theoretically, there <i>could </i>be some memories retained from life to life, but in practice, that's pretty rare - so while technically its the same being, in reality its effectively a whole new entity.<br /> <br /> The non-Scathach sidhe, on the other hand . . . well, they're closer to demonic possession. The sidhe &quot;soul&quot; kicks the human soul out of the body, which is (believed to be) sent to Arcadia. However, when that human body dies . . . well, no one really knows what happens to the sidhe soul. In Arcadia, the death of a sidhe was temporary. On Earth . . . no one's really sure. Many believe the non-Scathach sidhe truly die (although at least one appears to have become a banshee)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> can a changeling in his real form actually have a child with a human? or it needs to be with the human host? </div> </div> </div>Of course a changeling can have kids. There's a living, breathing human body in there, underneath all the glamour, perfectly capable of being impregnated (or getting someone pregnant).<br /> <br /> The catch is the child will either be a normal human, or kinain (a human with some fae &quot;blood&quot;) - not another fae. The impression I got (others may disagree) is that the number of faerie souls is fixed - at least on Earth. Maybe its a consequence of the changeling ritual, maybe of the increased banality of the world - but the changelings are literally a dying breed (although thanks to the reincarnation thing, they can stretch that out for millennia or more)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> does the Age of a Changeling shows on its human host or the human host can be very young while the actual changeling be ancient? </div> </div> </div>The age of the human body is reflected in the faerie &quot;seeming&quot; (i.e. form). So a thousand year old faerie soul awakening in a six-year-old's body will look (and act) like a six-year-old faerie. As others have mentioned, with the commoner and Scathach sidhe, its a bonding, a sharing - not a possession.<br /> <br /> There is a catch to this, though. Inside a freehold (the changeling equivalent to a node/caern/haunt), a changeling (or enchanted human) does <i>not</i> age, either physically or mentally. Sure, they can learn new skills . . . but they don't mature or &quot;grow up&quot;. There are sample NPCs in some of the <i>Changeling </i>supplements that have been frozen in time for decades (or more). So its theoretically possible to have a changeling who's chronologically over a thousand years old, but still looks/talks/acts like an eight-year-old.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T03:18:04-08:00","id":391198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/383876-questions-about-ctd?p=384008#post384008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One last question.<br /> <br /> a friend told me that Nightmares are quite brutal when it comes to Changeling. that they are particularly nasty when it comes to beings that use Glamour but they are not much of a threat against anything else..how can make a Nightmare that can actually be a threat against mages/werewolves and other supernaturals as well humans?</div> </div> </div> </div>Picking up on <b>Moirdryd</b>'s explanation:<br /> <br /> A NIghtmare is a type of chimera, a being made of pure glamour, spawned either by a particularly potent dream or certain forms of changeling magic. However, they have no mundane/&quot;physical&quot; body. As such, <i>most </i>chimera can't directly affect mundane reality - although they can (and do) interact with 'dual nature&quot; entities like changelings or enchanted humans. Some are glorious wonders, some are just nuisances, and some are quite freaky. And, needless to say, chimera spawned of nightmares aren't the nicest beings - some are merely creepy (like monsters-under-the-bed), while others are virtually demonic.<br /> <br /> So, as a rule, most humans (or other supernaturals) are immune to the machinations of Nightmares and other chimeras. They can't fly on a chimerical pegasus . . . but they also don't have to worry about a three-headed xenomorph-dragon using them as a chew toy, either. Unless a changeling enchants them, of course. <br /> <br /> However, certain mage rotes <i>et al</i> allow the user to perceive, and even interact with the denizens of the Dreaming . . . which makes them fair game for chimera (Nightmare or otherwise). And some places have special rules. Graymere Glen, for example, a changeling freehold, was the site of a human town for generations. The idea of one particular type of Nightmare (the Schnorrfleurs) became deeply ingrained in the residents, etched into their imagination generation after generation . . . resulting in the Schnorrfleurs actually being able to step into mundane reality in the area around the freehold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T04:25:41-08:00","id":391242,"title":"","content":"Some Chimera can also do stuff not unlike Banes in Werewolf influencing human emotion and action etc without ever having to Wyrd, those are the REALLY dangerous ones because there's basically no way to fight them without some kind of faerie magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T08:01:50-08:00","id":391444,"title":"","content":"I'd like to ask Changeling players.<br /> <br /> If it is about Pooka shapeshifting ability - I understand that mundane items are left behind. Does it mean that practically they are then seen at town as naked teenage boys after they change back from cat/fox to human?<br /> How to overcome it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3612,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","user":"Lunar","date":". 02-03-2015, 11:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","name":"Lunar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T08:42:08-08:00","id":391469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/383876-questions-about-ctd?p=391444#post391444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to ask Changeling players.<br /> <br /> If it is about Pooka shapeshifting ability - I understand that mundane items are left behind. Does it mean that practically they are then seen at town as naked teenage boys after they change back from cat/fox to human?<br /> How to overcome it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, being caught naked is a problem.<br /> <br /> As to solutions, a Pooka can cache their clothes somewhere before they change so they can come back and collect them, they can have a friend carry their clothes for them, or there's a Merit in the Pooka kithbook that allows you to include non-chimerical items in the transformation.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T08:47:45-08:00","id":391473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/383876-questions-about-ctd?p=391188#post391188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course a changeling can have kids. There's a living, breathing human body in there, underneath all the glamour, perfectly capable of being impregnated (or getting someone pregnant).<br /> <br /> The catch is the child will either be a normal human, or kinain (a human with some fae &quot;blood&quot;) - not another fae. The impression I got (others may disagree) is that the number of faerie souls is fixed - at least on Earth. Maybe its a consequence of the changeling ritual, maybe of the increased banality of the world - but the changelings are literally a dying breed (although thanks to the reincarnation thing, they can stretch that out for millennia or more).</div> </div> </div> </div>By the books, there's about a one-in-two chance the child of two changelings will be a changeling themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T06:31:17-08:00","id":392553,"title":"","content":"Is there a practical or narrative impact to the notion that sidhe possess, rather than meld with the soul of, the human body they inhabit? I understand they still are born and grow up for a while as a &quot;human,&quot; then undergo Chrysalis just like any other Changeling. And they don't recall their past any more than any other Changeling. So is it more than a declaration that yeah, they probably killed their host to take it over, or is there a sign other than that declaration in their behavior, nature, etc.?<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I don't recall seeing in the pooka description in the 2e core book that they don't take clothes with them. It has been a while, admittedly; is it in there, or is it written somewhere else and just ascribed to the kith once you know it's a rule?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T08:13:23-08:00","id":392619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/383876-questions-about-ctd?p=392553#post392553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a practical or narrative impact to the notion that sidhe possess, rather than meld with the soul of, the human body they inhabit? I understand they still are born and grow up for a while as a &quot;human,&quot; then undergo Chrysalis just like any other Changeling. And they don't recall their past any more than any other Changeling. So is it more than a declaration that yeah, they probably killed their host to take it over, or is there a sign other than that declaration in their behavior, nature, etc.?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... by Denizens of the Dreaming, it's established that it's more of a trade. The human soul replaced by the sidhe is taken back to Arcadia by a group of select keremet, which becomes a plot point in regards to one sidhe in the metaplot who wasn't supposed to enter the waking world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, I don't recall seeing in the pooka description in the 2e core book that they don't take clothes with them. It has been a while, admittedly; is it in there, or is it written somewhere else and just ascribed to the kith once you know it's a rule? </div> </div> </div>It's not in either of the corebooks or the Player's Guide. It's popped up by the kithbook, however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T09:27:02-08:00","id":392650,"title":"","content":"That kind of &quot;trade&quot; sounds like a Devil's Bargain at best. Is there negotiation or does it just happen? Can the human soul say &quot;no&quot;? What does the Sidhe have to offer? If it's &quot;Endless Wonder&quot; in exchange for &quot;Total Crap Life&quot; then Sidhe should be coming from crappy backgrounds, kinda like the Fallen. Otherwise, it seems like a bad seduction, where one party gets all the perks and the other side just gets screwed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T11:33:29-08:00","id":392791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/383876-questions-about-ctd?p=392650#post392650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That kind of &quot;trade&quot; sounds like a Devil's Bargain at best. Is there negotiation or does it just happen? Can the human soul say &quot;no&quot;? What does the Sidhe have to offer? If it's &quot;Endless Wonder&quot; in exchange for &quot;Total Crap Life&quot; then Sidhe should be coming from crappy backgrounds, kinda like the Fallen. Otherwise, it seems like a bad seduction, where one party gets all the perks and the other side just gets screwed.</div> </div> </div> </div>My interpretation of it - which, now I look at Denizens, wasn't backed up by the book - was that it was basically like the standard folklore changeling story, with the Sidhe switching (or being switched) for a human.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T06:51:10-08:00","id":393708,"title":"","content":"Now I'm even more unsure. Is this something that happens <i>instead</i> of a Chrysalis, with a human at whatever stage of growth being offered the trade and flat-out replaced in the middle of his life (where &quot;middle&quot; really means &quot;not at birth&quot;)? Or is this switch done at birth, like other Changelings have happen, but it is now a sidhe soul that mistakenly thinks its human until Chrysalis?<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure I've seen references in the core book to sidhe Chrysalises.<br /> <br /> What also continues to bug me is...is there a difference in any meaningful, you-can-tell-as-a-player sense between a sidhe who did the Changeling Way merging and a sidhe who kicked out the original human soul? Does one not have memories of being human?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T23:59:54-08:00","id":394561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/383876-questions-about-ctd?p=393708#post393708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I'm even more unsure. Is this something that happens <i>instead</i> of a Chrysalis, with a human at whatever stage of growth being offered the trade and flat-out replaced in the middle of his life (where &quot;middle&quot; really means &quot;not at birth&quot;)? Or is this switch done at birth, like other Changelings have happen, but it is now a sidhe soul that mistakenly thinks its human until Chrysalis?<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure I've seen references in the core book to sidhe Chrysalises.</div> </div> </div> </div>'Trade' was perhaps the wrong word to use, 'cause it implies that the human had a say in the matter. 'Switch' might have been better.<br /> <br /> Anyway. Having had a chance to look, the idea of the switch dates at least as far back as Nobles: the Shining Host, with the switch happening before the Chrysalis. The sidhe replaces the human soul, which gets taken to Arcadia (to the sidhe, it's like sponsoring an exchange student). Nobles implies that the time lapse before the sidhe's Chrysalis begins is typically very short, if not immediate.<br /> <br /> One consequence of the way the sidhe do things is that the common kith remember what it is to be human. The sidhe, however, only have faint and distant human memories, enough to fill them in on the life of the mortal they replaced.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What also continues to bug me is...is there a difference in any meaningful, you-can-tell-as-a-player sense between a sidhe who did the Changeling Way merging and a sidhe who kicked out the original human soul? Does one not have memories of being human? </div> </div> </div>Fortunately, House Scathach provides an illustration, having members who followed both of those courses of action. Members of the House who stayed on Earth find their kith Birthrights lessened, and require Fae Realm 1 to affect them (that is, they're treated as commoners for the purposes of cantrips). Members of the House who have recently returned to Earth have their kith Birthrights at full strength, and require Fae Realm 2, like other sidhe. Neither branch of House Scathach suffers Banality's Curse, so there's no way to tell what would happen to the Frailty.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T06:19:59-08:00","id":394727,"title":"","content":"Interesting. So yes, the real difference is that the Sidhe really never had a human life. He was a faerie noble in Arcadia, and then he arrived here and pretends to be somebody he isn't. Are their memories of Arcadia still intact, or are they here as amnesiacs who faintly recall their human life's broad strokes, and recall nothing of note of their Fae existence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T06:37:09-08:00","id":394737,"title":"","content":"No-one remembers Arcadia clearly.<br /> <br /> How much the sidhe remember of their past fae existence depends on their Remembrance, as it does for other kith, but unlike them the collective sidhe memory has a gaping hole in it, from the height of the Shattering, approximately 1349 CE, about the time of the Black Plague, to the Resurgence in 1969. The time the sidhe spent in Arcadia has disappeared from their memory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T08:13:04-08:00","id":394846,"title":"","content":"So...<br /> <br /> Sidhe don't remember a thing extra for having not spent any time as humans, but remember less about their human mask's life?<br /> <br /> Wow, they really do have the short end of that stick. They're basically clueless about all worlds they have lived in and currently do live in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T09:29:23-08:00","id":394999,"title":"","content":"And they are ripping people's souls and casting them into a realm of madness. (There has to be SOMETHING wrong with Arcadia. If it was ever so nice, why would the Sidhe want to come back to the dreary banal world of mortals? I know we can't know, because they can't remember, but the mass exodus doesn't suggest that it was a land of milk and honey, lotus eating and endless dancing or the like.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T10:52:50-08:00","id":395131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/383876-questions-about-ctd?p=394999#post394999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And they are ripping people's souls and casting them into a realm of madness. (There has to be SOMETHING wrong with Arcadia. If it was ever so nice, why would the Sidhe want to come back to the dreary banal world of mortals? I know we can't know, because they can't remember, but the mass exodus doesn't suggest that it was a land of milk and honey, lotus eating and endless dancing or the like.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Nobles suggested war, whether internal or external. The first Book of Houses suggested that the initial Houses been exiled for some reason they couldn't agree on (though House Gwydion suspected they'd chosen to come back to help others). In the second Book of Houses, House Leanhaun suggested they'd chosen to come back too, and that Arcadia had become seriously imbalanced towards Winter and the Unseelie. House Balor, meanwhile, suspected a Seelie power-grab that failed, resulting in the losers being exiled to Earth. In the third Book of Houses, House Beaumayn believed the stirring Fomorians had caused a sickness in the Dreaming, resulting in the Arcadians sending the Houses to Earth as a bail-out attempt, House Aerith thought an Ailil-headed uprising had been used as an excuse to send the original Houses back as agents in the Waking, and that the coming of the Fomorians saw the other Houses follow, House Daireann believes they're back to defend<i> somewhere</i> against the Fomorians, be it Earth or Arcadia, and House Varich thought Arcadia had stagnated in endless winter until the Fomorians announced their coming.<br /> <br /> We can reasonably guess that the Fomorians are why the final four Houses came to Earth, but why the initial eight Houses came is ambiguous.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T18:41:47-08:00","id":395738,"title":"","content":"So what powers and abilities might a Changeling have that could allow a changeling to interact with a Wraith? Can Changelings travel to the Low Umbra/Shadowlands?<br /> <br /> The wraith book mentions the following:<br /> -Changelings can occasionally see wraiths, particularly childlings that have not yet been taught that ghosts don't exist. (This is true of mortals as well)<br /> -Wraiths and Changelings sometimes compete for the same resources: Pathos and Glamour can sometimes be gained from the same source. The Sandmen Guild also gathers &quot;sand&quot; (pure dreamstuff) from dreamers which can thought of as another manifestation of Glamour.<br /> -Sluagh in particular will interact with wraiths, using them as spies sources of information. The book says that Sluagh can see into the Shadowlands with a perception + alterness roll, and can then converse freely with wraiths by expending a point of Glamour. Is this reflected in the C:tD books anywhere?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T23:31:31-08:00","id":395874,"title":"","content":"* According to the sluagh writeup in the Players Guide, they can see wraiths with a Perception+Alertness roll, and then speak with them by spending a point of Glamour. 2e's Book of Lost Dreams makes it a Perception+Kenning roll.<br /> * The Nunnehi have access to the Art of Spirit Link, allowing them to see and speak with wraiths, among other spirits (from the Players Guide).<br /> * The 2e corebook mentions that sometimes eshu are able to see wraiths. No mechanics, though.<br /> * Denizens of the Dreaming mentions the Black Paths of Balor, trods that lead from the Autumn Realm (ie, Earth) to the Shadowlands. Most fae avoid them, but sluagh and keremet both use them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T17:29:23-08:00","id":402650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/383876-questions-about-ctd?p=392650#post392650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That kind of &quot;trade&quot; sounds like a Devil's Bargain at best. Is there negotiation or does it just happen? Can the human soul say &quot;no&quot;? What does the Sidhe have to offer? If it's &quot;Endless Wonder&quot; in exchange for &quot;Total Crap Life&quot; then Sidhe should be coming from crappy backgrounds, kinda like the Fallen. Otherwise, it seems like a bad seduction, where one party gets all the perks and the other side just gets screwed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there's an old Irish/Celtic saying, about the sidhe being &quot;too good for hell, but not good enough for heaven&quot;. Pretty sure the game referenced it, too. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But no, the human doesn't really get a say in the matter. Maybe - maybe - a high willpower or high banality human could resist (<i>a la</i> demonic possession), but I don't think we ever saw mechanics for the process.<br /> <br /> However, the sidhe <i>believe</i> that the human souls are pampered in Arcadia - making it a &quot;fair&quot; exchange. . .which <i>is</i> in keeping with the spirit of traditional Celtic beliefs (i.e. the inspiration for the sidhe). Celtic magic (in folklore) was very reciprocal, with almost karmic retaliation for an &quot;unfair&quot; trade. So if you wanted to magically screw someone over, you had to trade them something they couldn't easily use (or didn't understand). Whether the sidhe are right or not (about the soul being pampered) is another question, though . . .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T18:03:26-08:00","id":402680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/383876-questions-about-ctd?p=393708#post393708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I'm even more unsure. Is this something that happens <i>instead</i> of a Chrysalis, with a human at whatever stage of growth being offered the trade and flat-out replaced in the middle of his life (where &quot;middle&quot; really means &quot;not at birth&quot;)? Or is this switch done at birth, like other Changelings have happen, but it is now a sidhe soul that mistakenly thinks its human until Chrysalis?<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure I've seen references in the core book to sidhe Chrysalises.<br /> <br /> What also continues to bug me is...is there a difference in any meaningful, you-can-tell-as-a-player sense between a sidhe who did the Changeling Way merging and a sidhe who kicked out the original human soul? Does one not have memories of being human?</div> </div> </div> </div>From a player's perspective, <b>Changeling: the Dreaming</b> gave us four &quot;flavors&quot; of sidhe on Earth:<br /> <br /> * Like commoner changelings, many members of House Scathach embraced the whole reincarnation/chrysalis method of survival on Earth, rather than withdrawing to Arcadia. As such, they are hybrid human/sidhe entities who have a full-fledged human life before the Chrysalis. Thanks to their human soul, they do <i>not</i> suffer Banality's Curse (the usual sidhe flaw) or any other special problems with banality. If slain (and given a wake), they reincarnate as Scathach sidhe.<br /> <br /> * Many of the first non-Scathach sidhe to return to Earth (post-moon landing) &quot;swapped&quot; with teen or adult humans - the better to establish a bulwark for their House. They immediately went into a very traumatic form of Chrysalis, as their faerie selves scrubbed the human personality from their new brain. They suffer (more or less) complete amnesia about the former human life, and people surrounding these &quot;first wave&quot; changelings often assumed they were having psychotic breaks, resulting in more than a few being institutionalized as mentally ill.<br /> <br /> The &quot;first wave&quot; sidhe suffer Banality's Curse (gaining &quot;bonus&quot; banality), and more. By the time of a default campaign (the Nineties) their &quot;skins had toughened&quot;, but many of the in-character pieces of fiction talk about how badly they were hit by banality in the early days of the Resurgence. One character (in <i>Nobles: the Shining Host</i>) even says that the &quot;first wave&quot; sidhe couldn't use modern technology (in the first days back) without being destroyed by banality.<br /> <br /> * Some of the early returners (and most of the later ones), on the other hand, swapped with very young children (even infants). So, while they don't have a human soul, these &quot;second wave&quot; sidhe had a &quot;human&quot; childhood (which they remember), with human &quot;parents&quot; <i>et al</i>. They're thus more comfortable with the human world and technology - but still suffer Banality's Curse.<br /> <br /> * Finally, the &quot;Immortal Eyes&quot; chronicle gave us a nasty version of the sidhe soul swap. Going into details involves spoilers, but the human soul was cast screaming into the void - not sent to Arcadia. Characters watching (even other sidhe) were horrified at the process, likening it to murder. Last I heard, only one sidhe has ever used this method, though - but its implied that it left him very susceptible to bedlam.<br /> <br /> And its worth pointing out that <i>only</i> the Scathach sidhe are known to reincarnate (again) as sidhe - at least from Earth. The other Houses, having not undergone the changeling ritual, either experience true death, or reincarnate as other sorts of (non-sidhe) fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T21:12:02-08:00","id":402959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And its worth pointing out that <i>only</i> the Scathach sidhe are known to reincarnate (again) as sidhe - at least from Earth. The other Houses, having not undergone the changeling ritual, either experience true death, or reincarnate as other sorts of (non-sidhe) fae. </div> </div> </div>Or their Souls escape back into the depths of the Dreaming as implied in many sources including multiple claims of some having seen the slain Sidhe's souls briefly as it flees into the Dreaming. It is deliberately been left somewhat unclear whether they suffer True Death, which they do in case of Cold Iron like everyone else, upon normal death though it is known that they do not reincarnate, apart from the exception you mentioned.<br /> <br /> But their Souls returning to the Dreaming is one very possible option so just adding it to your list.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T10:40:29-08:00","id":403441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/383876-questions-about-ctd?p=402650#post402650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, there's an old Irish/Celtic saying, about the sidhe being &quot;too good for hell, but not good enough for heaven&quot;. Pretty sure the game referenced it, too. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But no, the human doesn't really get a say in the matter. Maybe - maybe - a high willpower or high banality human could resist (<i>a la</i> demonic possession), but I don't think we ever saw mechanics for the process.<br /> <br /> However, the sidhe <i>believe</i> that the human souls are pampered in Arcadia - making it a &quot;fair&quot; exchange. . .which <i>is</i> in keeping with the spirit of traditional Celtic beliefs (i.e. the inspiration for the sidhe). Celtic magic (in folklore) was very reciprocal, with almost karmic retaliation for an &quot;unfair&quot; trade. So if you wanted to magically screw someone over, you had to trade them something they couldn't easily use (or didn't understand). Whether the sidhe are right or not (about the soul being pampered) is another question, though . . .</div> </div> </div> </div>You might be able to sell me on the first group of Houses and some naive vision of the place they left, since they seems relatively muddled about WHY they left it. So a lot of very mortal willfull ignorance about having done a very bad thing. Make up an plausible excuse that spins it your way and hold fast to it, even though it really doesn't stand up to even cursory scrutiny.<br /> <br /> But for the darker Houses? I don't buy that they thought they were ousting mortal souls and sending them to happy-happy-joy-joy land. They wouldn't have cared. And they really didn't DO happy-happy-joy-joy land to begin with. <br /> <br /> And the later mixed bag of Houses that are coming through with memories of fleeing the Fomor, aka the Nightmares of the Id, taking over the Dreaming? They had to KNOW they were exiling the human souls to a Hell that they were running screaming from. But, see &quot;willful ignorance&quot; above and also &quot;not giving a shit.&quot; <br /> <br /> We don't get any info that there was a bargain going on. In fact, it doesn't seem like there was. That's not like the middlish Celtic &quot;dealing with the Fair Folk&quot; stories. In those, you WOULD get screwed, if you weren't very careful, but you got to actually negotiate in the deal-making. So, leaving the Dreaming, popping a mortal soul out of its shell, inserting your fae self is a pretty crappy thing to do. Unless someone can track down a reference where it says that there was an actual negotiation? And, being a lawyerly type, &quot;actual negotiation&quot; means that the human could turn down the Sidhe. So I am asking if any of the CtD gurus out there know of an instance in which a Sidhe attempted to take a human host, but the human host said, &quot;No&quot; successfully.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T12:17:43-08:00","id":403587,"title":"","content":"While I do appreciate that there are, apparently, notable differences between sidhe who have and have not undergone the Changeling Way ritual, something about the idea that the sidhe have nothing of their &quot;human past&quot; about them does bug me.<br /> <br /> I think it's that it means that those who have any memories started invariably as childlings. I don't know quite why that bothers me, but it does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}